3) the (44) 1870s (45) whose (46) huge (47) front (48) wheel (49) offered (50) speed (51) but (52) little (53) safety.\n\nSentence 3: \"The modern bicycle emerged in 1885 with John Kemp Starley's Rover, the \"safety bicycle,\" which featured equal-sized wheels and a chain drive, and John Boyd Dunlop's pneumatic tires in 1888 greatly improved comfort.\" The (54) modern (55) bicycle (56) emerged (57) in (58) 1885 (59) with (60) John (61) Kemp (62) Starley's (63) Rover (64) the (65) safety (66) bicycle (67) which (68) featured (69) equal-sized (70) wheels (71) and (72) a (73) chain (74) drive (75) and (76) John (77) Boyd (78) Dunlop's (79) pneumatic (80) tires (81) in (82) 1888 (83) greatly (84) improved (85) comfort.\n\nSentence 4: \"These innovations transformed the bicycle from an eccentric contraption into a reliable, affordable machine that revolutionized personal transportation and, by the 1890s, sparked a global cycling craze.\" These (86) innovations (87) transformed (88) the (89) bicycle (90) from (91) an (92) eccentric (93) contraption (94) into (95) a (96) reliable (97) affordable (98) machine (99) that (100) revolutionized (101) personal (102) transportation (103) and (104) by (105) the (106) 1890s (107) sparked (108) a (109) global (110) cycling (111) craze.\n\nTotal: 112 words. Within 60-120 range. One paragraph, no headings or bullets. Good.\n\nStyle assessment: The paragraph flows chronologically, uses varied sentence structures, engaging language (\"eccentric contraption,\" \"boneshaker,\" \"cycling craze\"). Clear transitions. This is well-written. APPROVE.\n\nFirst word must be APPROVE or REVISE."},"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":254,"completion_tokens":945,"total_tokens":1199,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}}}

